@Harry — agreed, and thanks for catching this. You're right: the CloudFront flip only intercepts full page loads, so any legacy `routerLink` into a flipped path would keep showing the old page after the flip.

Let's make this a **per-page flag-on prerequisite**: for each path we flip, we'll (1) convert its legacy `routerLink`s to real `<a href>` full page navigations, and (2) remove the path from the Angular route table so a missed link fails loudly instead of silently serving legacy. We'll do it one page at a time, alongside each page's flag-on — starting with /privacy (the footer link).

No scope concern on the pilot side — the impact is small per page (footer link only for the legal pages). Thanks again.

